{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>As water, Sheol—</b> The meaning of 'as water' is water that has risen because of other water that mixes into it; so too face because of face. And the sense: like the heat of water, so the heart of man is full of evil, because of the man who hates him—and this is a correct interpretation. And he mentioned Sheol and Abaddon, for the enemies—their evil is in their heart; for naught they descend to them and they are never sated, and the eyes of man likewise are never sated to see, for when they gaze they go to Abaddon—do not say 'we are sated from seeing it and we will be chastened.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The opening lemma reads שאול ('Sheol') alongside כמים ('as water'), likely reflecting a textual variant or interpretive reading of the verse. The clause הולכין לאבדון is rendered hyper-literally; it is unclear whether the subject is the eyes or those observed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:06.394133487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}